@startuml deception-filesystem-P0C-TARGET
' =============================================================================
' STATUS: MIXED — read the per-tier status markers. NOTHING BELOW MARKED
'         "PROPOSED" OR "RECONSTRUCTION" IS DEPLOYED.
'
' Three distinct tiers, deliberately NOT merged, because conflating them is
' how a reconstruction quietly becomes fiction:
'
'   TIER 1  CURRENT_DEPLOYED          — verified on-host 2026-09-23
'   TIER 2  2025_TELEMETRY_EVIDENCED  — reconstructable from recovered corpus
'   TIER 3  PROPOSED_NOT_IMPLEMENTED  — design intent, no evidence, not built
'
' Evidence rule carried from the AuthParity gate: raw preserved corpus
' outranks paper summaries. Items the paper asserts but the corpus does NOT
' corroborate are recorded as insufficient authority and are NOT drawn as
' though they existed.
' =============================================================================

title Deception Filesystem — Current / Evidenced / Proposed (P0C)

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam roundcorner 6

legend top
  |= Tier |= Meaning |= Deployed? |
  | <back:#CCFFCC>TIER 1</back> | CURRENT_DEPLOYED — verified on host | YES |
  | <back:#FFF2CC>TIER 2</back> | 2025_TELEMETRY_EVIDENCED — direct corpus evidence | NO — target for P0C |
  | <back:#FFE0E0>TIER 3</back> | PROPOSED_NOT_IMPLEMENTED — design intent only | NO — no evidence |
endlegend

package "TIER 1 — CURRENT_DEPLOYED (stock Cowrie v2.5.0 fs.pickle)" #CCFFCC {
  card current [
  fs.pickle SHA-256 06f0ed52...
  Pinned by bootstrap-native.sh:287, which FAILS CLOSED on mismatch.
  Recognisable as the stock Cowrie tree to anyone who knows Cowrie.
  ----
  /  (23 top-level entries)
   ├── bin  boot  dev  etc  home  lib  media  mnt  opt
   ├── proc  root  run  sbin  selinux  srv  sys  tmp  usr  var
   ├── initrd.img   vmlinuz   lost+found
   └── **test2**            <-- stock-tree artifact, not ours
  ----
  /home/
   └── phil/                <-- ONLY user present
        ├── .bash_logout
        ├── .bashrc
        └── .profile
  ----
  honeyfs/ (contents layer) supplies bodies for:
   /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow, /etc/group, /etc/hosts, /etc/issue,
   /etc/motd, /etc/resolv.conf, /etc/inittab, /etc/host.conf,
   /proc/cpuinfo, /proc/meminfo, /proc/version, /proc/mounts,
   /proc/modules, /proc/net/arp, /home/admin/passwords.txt
  ----
  **CRITICAL**: honeyfs/ only supplies CONTENTS for paths that already
  exist in fs.pickle. /home/admin/passwords.txt is staged in honeyfs but
  **/home/admin does not exist in the pickle**, so it is unreachable.
  ]
}

package "TIER 2 — 2025_TELEMETRY_EVIDENCED (P0C restoration target)" #FFF2CC {
  card evidenced [
  Reconstructable from the recovered 2025 corpus — direct event evidence,
  not paper assertion.
  ----
  hostname / prompt:  **web-server-prod**
  ----
  /home/
   ├── admin/
   │    ├── .ssh/
   │    └── passwords.txt
   ├── backup/
   ├── deploy/
   │    └── config.json
   ├── lmenendez/
   ├── root/
   ├── webuser/
   └── wfingerdoo/
  ----
  /home/deploy/config.json returned:
    { "db_password": "prod2023!", "api_key": "sk-1234567890" }
  (historical synthetic canaries — fake by construction)
  ----
  **THE ACTUAL ATTACKER OBJECTIVE**, observed repeatedly across multiple
  unrelated source IPs:
    cd ~ ; chattr -ia .ssh ; lockr -ia .ssh
    rm -rf .ssh && mkdir .ssh
    echo "ssh-rsa ..." >> .ssh/authorized_keys
    chmod -R go= ~/.ssh
  ----
  cowrie.session.file_download emitted for attacker writes to:
    /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
    /home/admin/.ssh/authorized_keys
  ----
  => The 2025 environment did NOT need elaborate bait. It needed
     ~/.ssh to be present and manipulable, plus enough Linux
     semantics to support the chain above.
  ]
}

package "TIER 3 — PROPOSED_NOT_IMPLEMENTED (modern backend profile)" #FFE0E0 {
  card proposed [
  Design intent for a SEPARATE, versioned deception profile.
  NO telemetry evidence. NOT built. NOT deployed.
  Intended as an experimental lure variable AFTER parity is restored —
  never as a prerequisite for Cowrie functioning.
  ----
  /opt/app/
   ├── backend/{api,auth,core,db,integrations,middleware,
   │            models,services,workers,utils}/
   ├── config/{environments,feature_flags,logging}/
   ├── data/{cache,exports,imports,staging}/
   ├── migrations/   scripts/{maintenance,deployment,backfill}/
   ├── jobs/{scheduled,adhoc}/
   ├── logs/{api,worker,audit}/
   ├── backups/{daily,pre_migration}/
   ├── docs/{runbooks,architecture,api}/
   └── tmp/
  ----
  SaaS / AI-backend extension:
   /opt/app/{agent_runtime,model_gateway,evaluation,connectors,
             tool_registry,policy,telemetry,vectorstore,
             prompt_templates,workflows}/
  ----
  Accounting-persona extension:
   /home/{deploy,svc-api,jean,backup,ubuntu}/
   /srv/accounting/
   /opt/app/data/exports/{customer_export_2026-08.csv,
                          billing_reconciliation.csv}
   /opt/app/backups/pre_migration/{customer_db_20260901.sql.gz,
                                   accounting-prod.sql.gz}
  ----
  **CONSISTENCY REQUIREMENT**: fake values must agree ACROSS files.
  .env / DSNs / cloud identifiers / git remotes / audit logs must not
  contradict each other. An agent will notice if DATABASE_URL says
  PostgreSQL 15 while every runbook says MySQL 8.
  ]
}

package "EXCLUDED — insufficient reconstruction authority" #EEEEEE {
  card excluded [
  Asserted by the paper, **NOT** found in the recovered corpus on direct
  search. Deliberately NOT reconstructed.
  ----
    rat_loader_v5.py      paper_claim: yes  telemetry: NO
    db_dump.sql           paper_claim: yes  telemetry: NO
  ----
  classification: reconstruction_authority = INSUFFICIENT
  Rebuilding these would fabricate history, not restore it.
  ]
}

current -[#black]-> evidenced : **P0C** — restore evidenced parity first
evidenced -[#black]-> proposed : only AFTER parity verified;\nseparate versioned profile
excluded -[#gray,dashed]-> proposed : NOT carried forward

note bottom
  IMPLEMENTATION CONSTRAINT (from P0 recovery, evidence/2026-09-23-p0-recovery/):
  fs.pickle defines the NAMESPACE; honeyfs/ supplies CONTENTS only.
  Adding directories requires modifying fs.pickle — dropping files into
  honeyfs/ alone accomplishes nothing, as /home/admin/passwords.txt
  currently demonstrates.

  DELIVERY CONSTRAINT: bootstrap-native.sh is BootstrapBundleId -> UserData
  -> INSTANCE REPLACEMENT. Filesystem changes to the running sensor must
  ship via an SSM Association (AuthParity / H2 precedent), and the stock
  fs.pickle hash pin at bootstrap-native.sh:287 must be revised in the same
  change or it will fail closed.
end note

@enduml
